From 0d14adeb3319abf1a81762e61e2e1169a826dc70 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: davmels <davmelous@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 06:11:16 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Apertus 2 format: encode prompts to IDs and grade one output
 frame

A model trained on the Apertus 2 message format has no chat template: its
prompts are built from typed messages, and its outputs are frames that only
token IDs can split safely. Selected by config, so other models are unchanged.

- apertus2_math_data_processor encodes the prompt with apertus-common.
- policy.generation.output_format=apertus2 applies the format's token mask in
  vLLM and parses each output from its token IDs.
- env.math.reward_frame picks the graded frame, claim or reply. The other is
  verified too, and frames/* metrics and val_data_step*.jsonl compare them.
